{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms","id":1139838,"title":"Reform and Materialize charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-12T22:47:48-07:00","id":1139838,"title":"Reform and Materialize charms","content":"So, W20 left me wondering...<br /> <br /> <u>Materialize</u>: a Nexus Crawler materialzies with 12 health levels. It's supposed to be a lot, so I assume that an ordinary spirit only materializes with 7? This would mean that even a strong 40 essence spirit is going to have its life points seriously reduced in the material world (after 7 damage he's sent into Slumber, while in the Umbra he could take up to 40 points).<br /> <br /> <u>Re-form</u>: a spirit can teleport away instantly, no question asked, if he only manages to roll Gnosis. It feels a bit too good and powerful... is there any Gift or technique around that can stop a spirit from escaping? Otherwise I can't imagine how you could even attempt to bind one of these guys by force in a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T03:34:16-07:00","id":1139866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms#post1139838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, W20 left me wondering...<br /> <br /> <u>Materialize</u>: a Nexus Crawler materialzies with 12 health levels. It's supposed to be a lot, so I assume that an ordinary spirit only materializes with 7? This would mean that even a strong 40 essence spirit is going to have its life points seriously reduced in the material world (after 7 damage he's sent into Slumber, while in the Umbra he could take up to 40 points).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would easily give 15 health levels to a materialized Nexus Crawler, with 4 brawl, 6 dexterity, 10 strength and stamina, a warp reality action per turn and extra attacks at least as much as the enemies that surround it, speciffically for this big bad dood I would even increase the damage difficulty to hurt it. Maybe 8-9 or 10 if it used warp reality for defense instead of offense, not to mention tha all its damage should be usoakable because it is made of raw entropy. Just because you are close to it you must take damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T04:59:53-07:00","id":1139878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms#post1139838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (after 7 damage he's sent into Slumber, while in the Umbra he could take up to 40 points).</div> </div> </div> </div>After 7 damage the material body is destroyed and the spirit returns to Umbra. To put the spirit into slumber you would have to follow it back into the umbra and continue to fight it like normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms#post1139838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a spirit can teleport away instantly</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not true, this requires one full turn to take effect. If you are trying to bind a spirit by force its not supposed to be easy. Garou have pacts with spirits to avoid having to force one into a fetish.<br /> <br /> That said, their are Theurage gifts which allow them to command and disorient spirits for that it is difficult for them to escape. These gifts are normally used on malevolent spirits but could be used on any spirit.<br /> <br /> There are other ways such as Sorcery and gaining the help of a more powerful spirit which can be used as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T12:56:42-07:00","id":1140289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms?p=1139878#post1139878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After 7 damage the material body is destroyed and the spirit returns to Umbra. To put the spirit into slumber you would have to follow it back into the umbra and continue to fight it like normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, pag 366 of core manual: &quot;If a spirit dies in the material world, it returns to the Umbra and enters Slumber, just as if the spirit had lost all of its Essence in the Umbra&quot;. So it's extra dangerous for them to be on that side of the gauntlet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T14:33:29-07:00","id":1140316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms?p=1140289#post1140289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, pag 366 of core manual: &quot;If a spirit dies in the material world, it returns to the Umbra and enters Slumber, just as if the spirit had lost all of its Essence in the Umbra&quot;. So it's extra dangerous for them to be on that side of the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is new or we have been doing it wrong for a long time. That makes it even easier to wear out a spirit then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T14:52:12-07:00","id":1140324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1139838-reform-and-materialize-charms?p=1140316#post1140316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that is new or we have been doing it wrong for a long time. That makes it even easier to wear out a spirit then.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's relatively new. Not sure if it was that way in Revised or not, but I know before that it wasn't. The spirit also used to get to decide how many health levels it wanted when materializing which they don't seem to get to anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T07:28:32-07:00","id":1140511,"title":"","content":"Eh, spirits got a couple of mods in W20. Just to mention another, now you can permanently destroy spirits by ravaging them after causing their slumber, while in 2nd edition they were virtually invincible (in fact dangerous spirits were usually bound somewhere rather than killed - unless they were sent to Malfeas or engaged by Celestines, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T08:51:32-07:00","id":1140530,"title":"","content":"That kinda screws up the Setting as written though, since now there is no reason to have bound those spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:19:37-07:00","id":1140542,"title":"","content":"I know, right? Half of the work the Uktena did feels odd now.<br /> But this is the paragraph:<i> &quot;A spirit that runs out of Essence slowly fades into the Umbra. Garou can harvest Gnosis from such spirits, bringing them to a permanent end, or bind them into fetishes. Without a werewolf\u2019s interference, the spirit must rebuild its Essence before rematerializing in the Umbra.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Gnosis harvesting is interesting, but I'm not sure if I want spirit permakills. Of course, now you can reduce the greed in the whole world by simple killing a Greed incarna and Gaian spirits can be killed too, so it's not like there are only downsides. I'd like to talk to the W20 authors to hear their reasons for changing this though, I'm quite curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}